From 58e7c4914dbcde4763e2dd70cf02cb26710110a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 11:24:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] securize: rework to property-based toggle with GSI 
 fingerprint tracking

release builds: add pstore-visible stage markers around the securize
path so a boot that never dismisses the bootanimation leaves its last
completed stage in console-ramoops, readable from recovery with no adb
authorization. move the usb gadget string rewrite from the post-fs
securize path into phh-on-boot: configfs is not guaranteed to be
mounted that early, so the rewrite silently no-op'd on a long tail of
devices, and it does not need to sit in the boot-critical path.

